 "rationale": "Correction to round 2: dBbar is removed. Since Jx^2 + (Jy-Jz)^2/2 + (Jy+Jz)^2/2 = J2, sym(w[1,1] J2) is exactly A + B + C, which is the linear dependence the independent_terms certificate reported. An average rotor shift remains available through the rotor terms. I found no other dependency by hand: sigma and sigmaJ differ by the J(J+1) factor, gz and gxy are different J components on the regular orbit of the ordered pair (1,3), and gopp acts on opposite-well pairs. Wells and phase: each of the 6 C2v wells has one long-bond pair, and its hole function is the F2 combination along that pair's H-H direction, giving (0,1,+-1), (1,0,+-1), (1,+-1,0) over sqrt2, up to a free sign. The stabilizer of well 1 is {E, C2x, sigma(y=z), sigma(y=-z)}, with signs +,-,+,-. The induced representation is therefore F1+F2 rather than the unsigned A1+E+F2. This matches the data: N+=0 appears only as F2, with no N+=0 A or E line, while N+=1,2,3 carry A1, A2, E and F, as (F1+F2) x D(N) predicts. Rotor axes for well 1: the C2 axis x carries A; the long-pair direction (0,1,1) has the largest moment and carries C; the short-pair direction (0,1,-1) carries B. A hand estimate from the xyz supports this, with I about 2.4, 3.2 and 4.4 amu A^2. Tunneling: the saddle's permutation (13) with reflection links wells whose long pairs share one atom, so w[1,3] is the nearest-well hop over the 12 octahedron edges. sigma(x=y) exchanges wells 1 and 3 with sign product +1, so the term is Hermitian. In this gauge v1.v3 = -1/2, so H_ij = -2 sigma (v_i.v_j) on the edges. The off-diagonal Gram matrix has eigenvalues +1 (F2) and -1 (F1), which gives F2 at -2 sigma and F1 at +2 sigma for positive sigma. F2 is lowest, as Ham's theorem expects, with F1-F2 splitting 4 sigma. Pure opposite-well hopping w[1,2] vanishes by the conflicting stabilizer signs and is omitted. Extras, checked by hand: sigmaJ is the J dependence of tunneling; gz and gxy use J components odd under sigma(x=y), so with the factor i they are Hermitian and time-reversal even; gopp is allowed by C2x, both sigma_d planes and S4x. The B/C assignment and the sign of sigma are physical arguments. Whether the calibration preserves the sign of sigma is an assumption. This spec has not been run through the compiler or fitted.",
